{
  "about": "planter's flows as deploy drivers (M233): planter-prod (the pull request that readies an app for prod), planter-go-live (its pointer, live at <name>.apps.arugula.io), planter-ship (an agent's tarball onto loam) and planter-promote (the pull request that moves a shipped app into the cluster). Names: a prod name is a host label of at most 42 (lowercase letters, digits, dashes, not first or last); a shipped app's at most 32 and not reserved (the platform's, planter's, Flux's and the org's own names). Sources: Ship an artifact by its digest (sha256:<64 lowercase hex>) from the platform's store, the others a commit by its full id; Prod and Go live of arugula-salad/<app>, Promote of arugula-salad/shipped. The renderer's digest, named in every plan, is SHA-256 over each vendored file's path, a zero byte, its bytes and a zero byte, in the order platform-app/render.mjs, prod-scaffold.mjs, renderer.mjs (the files are crates/e2e/src/planter/). Settings and plans are in drivers/.",
